2026-11-11T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2490) 'What the fabric is for, and what it is not
 # uuid: 2ddd6de8-4f41-5021-b1b2-dc288e9c104a
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-11T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2490) 'the whole RFD board: its purpose and its non-goals.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2490) 'Does a new RFD on this board serve the open, self-hosted campus, or does it drift toward a walled garden?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The 2020 charter asked for an open, remixable, self-hosted VR space. Most of it still holds. The targets and the trust model have moved on.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2490) 'Check a new idea against the non-goals in the details. A match is refused, not argued again.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2490) 'Charter digest and board-wide non-goals
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2490) 'We work on the important problem, the one with a reasonable attack, and we stop work that serves no important problem (Hamming, "You and Your Research", 1986). We maximize our use cases and minimize our work and tools (operator, 2026-11-25). Today the important problem is the first beta (RFD66606-2360), set out in the details. The board-wide non-goals below bind every RFD on this board (operator, 2026-11-11).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2490) '- RFD66606-2360, the campus beta, which points here for its non-goals.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2490) '- RFD66606-2146, bao is the secret store.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2490) '- RFD66606-2202, ReBAC role tuples enforced via Bao identity groups.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2490) '- The 2020-06-08 V-Sekai charter, at https://v-sekai.github.io/manuals/decisions/20200608-vsekai-charter.html.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The fabric and its first beta
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The fabric is an open, remixable, self-hosted collaborative space built on Godot. Its first beta: two people in one campus zone see each other's avatars, one on a win64 desktop and one on another win64 desktop (operator, 2026-11-26). The beta is one platform, one guest host with one message shape and one build path. The client ships as a win64 ORAS folder and each server as a NixOS flake container under Ankaios (operator, 2026-11-26).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2490) 'Charter digest
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The 2020 Mozilla MVP application (https://v-sekai.github.io/manuals/decisions/20200608-vsekai-charter.html) set out these intents.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: a remixable, self-hosted, collaborative VR environment on Godot Engine.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: openness and communication as the basis of the platform.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: an open alternative to walled-garden social VR.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: users keep power over their data and can run the platform privately.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: easy to compile and modify.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: baseline presence, people in a room who can see each other (beta 1). Hearing each other rides on the platform as a use case (RFD66606-2360, operator, 2026-11-25).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Kept: a neutral host for events, and for business meetings where privacy matters.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Superseded: Windows SteamVR and Oculus Quest as targets. The targets are win64 on Windows. The Steam Frame and the Steam Deck were dropped as targets (operator, 2026-11-26). The Mac is not a target (operator, 2026-11-26).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Superseded: decentralized authentication through a GPG web of trust. OpenBao is the identity and secret store (operator, 2026-11-11; see RFD66606-2146 and RFD66606-2202).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Superseded: BitTorrent and IPFS distribution. Content ships from a standard CDN through HTTP range requests, chunked so that desync-compatible tools can fetch it (operator, 2026-11-11).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Dropped: the 2020 stack (k3s, CentOS 8, Digital Ocean Spaces), the eight-week Gantt chart, team bios and user-count estimates.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Not promised here: end-to-end encryption between users. OpenBao does not provide it, and nothing in this board commits to it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2490) 'Board-wide non-goals
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2490) 'A non-goal on this board is abandoned, not deferred. A new RFD that matches one is refused, and the list is not argued again.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A paywall at the door: no licence, sponsor or membership check in the client or the server.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A client for a phone or a web page.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Fly as a host for any server piece (operator, 2026-11-12).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2490) '- FEX, the x86 emulation layer, as a runtime for any build (operator, 2026-11-12).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Proton, the third-party compatibility layer (operator, 2026-11-12).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The beta's own non-goals are listed once, in RFD66606-2360.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2490) 'How the board picks its work
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2490) 'The board picks work the way Hamming's "You and Your Research" (1986, https://www.cs.virginia.edu/~robins/YouAndYourResearch.html) says a researcher does (operator, 2026-11-25).
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A problem is important when it has a reasonable attack. A problem with no attack is a non-goal, however large its consequence.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2490) '- The beta's important problem is the one the gate of RFD66606-2436 holds. Each session says which important problem its work serves and what its attack is.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A session whose work serves no important problem stops or changes its goal, whatever work it has already started.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Doors stay open. A session says what it works on and what it needs, and reads what the others say.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2490) '- A slice of the effort goes to the bigger question: is the gate still the important problem?
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Unknowns stay on the page. Each RFD's "What is not known" and each planted-defect control is the list of evidence against the work.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-11T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2490) '- Work is done so that others can build on it. A document comes before the code.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2490  1 LINE
 Text:Written
